                        late 14th-cent. College inventory-mark 37’ liber theologie is on 3; another,
                        9 liber theologie, erased from 2v (an unusual place for it); so it was after
                        that date that the book went astray, and had later to be recovered by Bishop
                        Gray.’ (Mynors, Balliol, 30)</p></provenance>
